## Author of Latest Modifications (`cmix-neif-3.1`)

* **Copyright (C) 2026 Oleksandr Dreval**
  * GitHub Profile: <https://github.com/OleksandrDreval>
  * Project Repository: <https://github.com/OleksandrDreval/cmix-neif-3.1>
  * Scope of copyright & GPL-3.0 section 5a modifications (November 2026):
    1. Stage-2 self-extracting stub `systrap` warm-up fix, stage-1 bootstrap
       context-mixer re-tuning, and low-memory (`1.51 GiB` peak RSS) sequential
       packer build & bit-exact verification (`tools_src/packer/stub.c`,
       `tools_src/packer/boot_models.h`, `tools_src/packer/build_packer.sh`,
       `build_and_construct_comp.sh`).
    2. Lossless `.c5` transformer weight container entropy-coding upgrades
       (Sign-Magnitude `ENC_INT4W`, per-canonical-name probability tables,
       refined width bucketing, counting `ENC_BF16C` high-byte trees, empirical
       QAT bimodal sparsity priors in `FrischInt4`, cross-tensor warm-start
       priors `CopyWarmCN`, Bayesian column pseudocount `pr_c = 40`, two-stage
       `bfloat16` lo-byte adaptation shifts, and `last_zrow` skipping of zero
       scales and dead KDA `key_convolution.weight` rows) and re-encoded
       `3,737,194 B` container `weights-poc8m_w2048_tf2t3_pruned_v5k_np2.c5`
       (`src/tf1/`, `src/transformer.h`,
       `training/tf/3_train/export/np2/tf1_np_codec.cpp`).
    3. `BITLSTM` slot-1 3-bit mantissa rounding, `kBlobW` nibble right-shift
       alignment, and 100 % IEEE-754 bit-exact frozen AVX2 inference fast-path
       with register-preloaded `Dot32Preloaded` and transposed non-FMA `hidP`
       projection (`src/bit_head_weights.h`, `src/bit_head.cpp`).
    4. ~2.86x peak RAM reduction across the `PPMd` page pool (`zonen_textrahmen`
       `4 MiB` rounding fix, demand-paged `memfd`), single-mapping demand-paged
       `SEMCACHE` (`MAP_NORESERVE` + `FreeFxcmRest` `munmap` with exact
       `kNLog = 24, kB = 18` SimHash geometry, `RunCompression` cleanup) and
       4 KiB demand-paged `arena` / `HugeBuf` allocators, plus 4-row AVX2
       unrolling in `SemDotPm1` (`src/models/ppmd*.{h,cpp}`,
       `src/semantic_cache.h`, `src/predictor.cpp`, `src/runner.cpp`,
       `src/arena_alloc.h`, `src/tf1/opt/arena_build.cpp`).
    5. Compiler warning cleanups and PGO diagnostic flags across `src/` and
       `makefile`, plus analytical/benchmark documentation
       (`en-optimization_report_it_1.md`, `en-optimization_report_it_2.md`,
       `uk-optimization_report_it_1.md`, `uk-optimization_report_it_2.md`,
       `CHANGES.md`, `NOTICE.md`, `README.md`, `training/`).

No copyright claim is made by Oleksandr Dreval over inherited upstream code;
his copyright claim covers the `cmix-neif-3.1` modifications and reports only,
licensed under `GPL-3.0-only`.

